{
  "title": "Overlapping Toe",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4080/overlapping-toe",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 15 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Overlapping Toe is a rare congenital condition caused by contraction of the extensor digitorum longus in children that presents with a digit that overlaps another.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with adduction and slight external rotation of the affected digit while overlapping another digit.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually passive stretching and buddy taping. Surgery management is indicated for patients who fail nonoperative treatment and remains symptomatic.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "evenly distributed between males and females",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the fifth toe most commonly affected",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "usually bilateral",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
